The portable C in the scenario start-setup: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/start-setup.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 10, 14, 29 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the box of F10 names the program in its title and in its question, by a
name that is two letters shorter: the box is two cells narrower, a cell on
either side, and its shadow ends a cell further left. Where the box is over
what DOS had shown, with no panel on the left, the cell that it no longer
covers on the left shows what DOS wrote there: the banner, as the portable C
has it, and the commands. And the Advanced options have no Quick execute
commands: Clear keyboard buffer and what is below it in the box stand a row
further up, the cursor with them where it is on that box, the box is a row
shorter, and the two rows that its last row and the shadow below it were on
show what is behind the box, the upper one in the shadow. And the panel that
the program has without a setup file, and with one that is not correct, is
sorted by name where the original's is unsorted: the list on C:\WORK in the
order of the names; the Right menu on it a row shorter, without Unsorted, with
Name ticked; and the setup file that the defaults leave has 0 for the order of
both panels where the original's has 8

